      ],
      "source": "https://www.tobinhill.org/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood covers roughly 700 acres just north of downtown San Antonio, a sizable suburban enclave.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tclf.org/tobin-hill",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Development kicked off in 1877 when Colonel Augustus Belknap built a horse railroad from Houston Street to San Pedro Springs Park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tobinhill.org/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Although land was distributed by lottery as early as 1777, actual settlement didn’t begin until the late 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tobinhill.org/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Tobin Hill’s streets follow a planned rectilinear subdivision, a design choice highlighted by the Texas Center for Landscape Architecture.",
